      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "marginalia_0",
      "quote": "A systematic review and meta-analysis of antimicrobial resistance knowledge, attitudes, and practices: Current evidence to build a strong national antimicrobial drug resistance narrative in Ethiopia.",
      "reason": "The title explicitly identifies the report as a \"systematic review and meta-analysis\"."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "marginalia_0",
      "quote": "A systematic review and meta-analysis of antimicrobial resistance knowledge, attitudes, and practices: Current evidence to build a strong national antimicrobial drug resistance narrative in Ethiopia.",
      "reason": "The title clearly states the review topic (antimicrobial resistance knowledge, attitudes, and practices) and the population/context (Ethiopia)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "marginalia_0",
      "quote": "A systematic review and meta-analysis of antimicrobial resistance knowledge, attitudes, and practices: Current evidence to build a strong national antimicrobial drug resistance narrative in Ethiopia.",
      "reason": "The title includes \"meta-analysis,\" which provides relevant supplementary information regarding the analysis method used."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_20",
      "quote": "To begin with, researchers have described that irrational antimicrobial prescribing and dispensing practices in low- and middle-income countries, Ethiopia included, are frequently attributed to a lack of knowledge about AMR [43, 44]. ... As a result, approximately only half (52%) of Ethiopians had a good level of knowledge about AMR. When participants' characteristics are stratified, the general population (43.92%), patients visiting healthcare facilities (42.73%), and livestock producers (27.11%) had a lower level of good knowledge of AMR.",
      "reason": "The text describes the current state of knowledge regarding AMR in Ethiopia, highlighting specific gaps in knowledge among different population groups."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a silent pandemic that has claimed millions of lives, and resulted in long-term disabilities, limited treatment options, and high economic costs associated with the healthcare burden. Given the rising prevalence of AMR, which is expected to pose a challenge to current empirical antibiotic treatment strategies, we sought to summarize the available data on knowledge, attitudes, and practices regarding AMR in Ethiopia.",
      "reason": "The authors explain the importance of the topic (AMR as a silent pandemic) and the need for the review (to summarize data on knowledge, attitudes, and practices in Ethiopia given the rising prevalence of AMR)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_20",
      "quote": "This systematic review and meta-analysis is the first of its kind and presents the most comprehensive assessment of the level of good knowledge, favorable attitudes, and good practices toward AMR.",
      "reason": "The authors explicitly state that this is the first systematic review of its kind, thereby addressing the requirement to explain the need for the review in the context of existing (or lack of) similar reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of observational studies on knowledge, attitudes, and practices (KAP), not a review of intervention effects."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of observational studies on knowledge, attitudes, and practices (KAP), not a review of complex interventions or delivery contexts requiring a logic model."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Therefore, we sought to summarize available data on good knowledge, favorable attitudes, and good practices toward AMR.",
      "reason": "The review explicitly states its objective in the introduction: to summarize available data on knowledge, attitudes, and practices toward AMR. While it does not use a formal question-formulation framework (like PICO) for the objective statement itself, the objective is clearly and explicitly stated."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is not a review of intervention effects; it is a systematic review and meta-analysis of prevalence data (knowledge, attitudes, and practices), so PICO comparisons are not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "Population/Participants : Weincluded primary studies involving various participants (patients, the general population, healthcare workers, livestock producers, and tertiary-level students). Condition : This systematic review and meta-analysis considered studies that had measured the outcome of interest based on knowledge, attitudes, and practices toward AMRand /or factors associated with them. Context/settings : All observational epidemiological studies (case-control, cohort, and cross-sectional) conducted in Ethiopia",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies the population (patients, general population, etc.), the condition (knowledge, attitudes, and practices toward AMR), and the study designs (case-control, cohort, and cross-sectional) and setting (Ethiopia)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "published in English between January 2010 and December 2022 in international and domestic peerreviewed journals were included. Furthermore, studies without full-text access; ... unpublished data were excluded.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies language (English), publication date range (January 2010 to December 2022), and publication status (peer-reviewed journals, excluding unpublished data)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not explicitly distinguish between exclusion due to outcomes not being measured versus exclusion due to outcome results not being reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "In addition, sensitivity and subgroup meta-analyses were performed.",
      "reason": "While the manuscript mentions that subgroup meta-analyses were performed, it does not explicitly define the groups used in each synthesis or link them to the comparisons defined in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The manuscript does not provide specific rationales for the restrictions on study eligibility (e.g., why only English language or why only studies from 2010-2022)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

